{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Built and locally exercised a five-voter harness for the stale-configuration safety question: it reproduces the configuration gap on a multi-node history (the node restarts from a three-voter snapshot while its log already holds the committed re-promotion entry) and reaches leadership via the repository's own transfer API, but its final attribution step is not yet sound locally because the restarted node's replication set did not match its stale voter set, so the producer that changed its configuration before runLeader is still unidentified. I therefore only sharpened that question's hypothesis and discriminator (comparing live configuration with the actual replication set before attributing any acknowledged-write consequence) and submitted no experiment or measurement as evidence.\"}"}}
